SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Triada\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora (Messaria)\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of the two feasts Kythnos itself names as its most important: Agia Triada in Chora\, on the eve and day of Agiou Pnevmatos (Whit Monday). The pattern is the island's classic — vespers\, then an all-night glenti with local violin and laouto players and the Kythnian 'balos' dance in the square\, continuing after the morning liturgy. Chora is a 10-minute drive from Merichas\; the square fills\, so come at dusk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#chora-messaria-panigiri-of-agia-triada-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#chora-messaria-panigiri-of-agia-triada-chora
